---
import Header from "@/components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "@/components/Footer.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "@/components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { SITE } from "@/config";
---

<Layout
  title={`Privacy Policy · Pourveyor | ${SITE.title}`}
  description="Ramon Claudio, LLC · Pourveyor Privacy Policy"
>
  <Header />
  <Breadcrumb />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="app-prose mb-28 max-w-app prose-img:border-0">
      <h1 class="text-2xl tracking-wider sm:text-3xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Ramon Claudio, LLC · Pourveyor</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last Updated: July 30, 2026</p>

      <p>
        Ramon Claudio, LLC ("we," "our," or "us") operates the Pourveyor mobile
        application. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and
        protect your information.
      </p>

      <h3>Browsing Without an Account</h3>
      <p>
        You can browse every shop, map, and detail page without signing in. No
        account is required, and we collect no personal information from you
        until you choose to create one.
      </p>

      <h3>Information We Collect</h3>
      <p>If you create an account, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account information:</strong> name, username, email address, avatar,
          and bio you provide during sign-up or profile editing
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Authentication data:</strong> hashed password (Argon2), Apple Sign
          In identifier, active session tokens, and one-time verification codes
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Push notification token:</strong> APNs device token registered on
          sign-in, along with the device type, used only to deliver notifications
          to that device
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>What We Do Not Collect</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          No analytics and no crash reporting. The app ships no analytics or
          crash-reporting SDK.
        </li>
        <li>No advertising identifiers, and no tracking across apps or sites</li>
        <li>No search history. Search runs on your device and is not recorded.</li>
        <li>
          No payment information. The app has no purchases and no subscriptions.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Location</h3>
      <p>
        The map asks for location access so it can show where you are relative
        to the shops. Your location is used on your device by Apple Maps to draw
        that indicator and nothing else. It is never sent to our servers, never
        stored, and never shared. You can decline the prompt or turn access off
        in iOS Settings, and every other part of the app keeps working.
      </p>

      <h3>How We Use Your Information</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>To authenticate your identity and manage your sessions</li>
        <li>
          To deliver email verification codes, password resets, and email-change
          confirmations
        </li>
        <li>To deliver push notifications when relevant events occur</li>
        <li>To store the profile you create in the app</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Third-Party Services</h3>
      <p>We use the following third-party services:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Convex (backend, real-time data, file storage)</li>
        <li>Better Auth (authentication and session management)</li>
        <li>Resend (transactional email delivery)</li>
        <li>
          Apple App Store and Apple Push Notification service (distribution and
          notifications)
        </li>
        <li>Apple Sign In (optional authentication provider)</li>
        <li>Apple Maps (map rendering, directions, and Look Around)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These services have their own privacy policies governing their use of
        your data. Opening directions or Look Around hands off to Apple Maps,
        which is covered by Apple's privacy policy, not this one.
      </p>

      <h3>Apple Sign In</h3>
      <p>
        If you sign in with Apple, you may choose to share your real email or
        use Apple's Hide My Email relay. Either way, we receive a stable user
        identifier from Apple and the email address you elect to share. We do
        not receive your Apple ID password.
      </p>

      <h3>Data Sharing</h3>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We share data only with the
        third-party services listed above as necessary to operate the app.
      </p>

      <h3>Data Retention and Deletion</h3>
      <p>
        Your data is retained for as long as your account is active. You may
        delete your account at any time from Profile → Delete Account. Deletion
        starts a 30-day grace window during which you can sign back in and
        restore the account. After 30 days your profile, sessions, and push
        tokens are permanently removed.
      </p>

      <h3>Security</h3>
      <p>
        We use industry-standard security measures to protect your data,
        including TLS for all transport, Argon2 for password hashing, signed
        Apple Sign In tokens, rate-limited authentication endpoints, and short
        session lifetimes with automatic refresh. You can review and revoke
        individual devices from the active sessions screen.
      </p>

      <h3>Children's Privacy</h3>
      <p>
        Pourveyor is not intended for children under 13. We do not knowingly
        collect personal information from children under 13.
      </p>

      <h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be
        posted on this page and reflected in the "Last Updated" date.
      </p>

      <h3>Contact Us</h3>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact us at
        <a href="mailto:team@ramonclaudio.com">team@ramonclaudio.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
